{"id":"q29","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"logic","question":"All roses are flowers. Some flowers fade quickly. Does it logically follow that some roses fade quickly?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"Roses are a kind of flower, so some roses might share what is true of some flowers.","confidence":0.3,"lean":0.6,"theta":0.4712,"phi":0.6573},{"text":"It is tempting to infer that some roses fade quickly.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.3,"theta":1.2566,"phi":2.9345},{"text":"The premises do not guarantee that the quick-fading flowers include any roses.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.0345},{"text":"The flowers that fade quickly could be a subset lying entirely outside the rose category.","confidence":0.92,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4451,"phi":3.0605},{"text":"A scenario where all roses last for months and only tulips and daisies fade quickly makes both premises true.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.0641},{"text":"In that scenario no rose fades quickly, so the conclusion is false while the premises are true.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.95,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.0624},{"text":"Because the premises can be true with a false conclusion, the conclusion does not logically follow.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":3.0603},{"text":"Everyday plausibility of the conclusion is irrelevant to logical validity.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.0589}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.2,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":6,"J":